========================================================================
POST-RACE UPDATE WORKFLOW (2026 SEASON)
========================================================================

## STEP 1: UPDATE F1 DATA (AUTOMATED)

Run the api_update.py script to automatically fetch and update all F1 data:

    cd src/config/f1
    py api_update.py

This will update the following files in src/config/f1/:
  - results.json        (race results for every completed round)
  - qualifying.json     (qualifying session results with Q1/Q2/Q3 times)
  - sprint.json         (sprint race results for sprint weekends only)
  - races/races.json    (race calendar with meeting keys)
  - races/2026/driverStandings.json
  - races/2026/constructorStandings.json
  - drivers/*.json      (per-driver career statistics)
  - constructors/       (constructor and driver rosters)

*Note: The script includes rate-limit retry logic. A full run may take a few minutes.

## STEP 1b: UPDATE F2 & F1A DATA (MANUAL)

These still need to be updated manually:
  - F2:  src/config/f2/results.json
  - F1A: src/config/f1a/results.json

*Note: For F2/F1A, remember to add Sprint points directly to the 'points' field in results.json!
       For F1, the API returns combined points (race + sprint + fastest lap) automatically.

## STEP 2: REBUILD & EXPORT DATA

1. Run Rebuild: Visit http://localhost:3000/api/admin/rebuild-2026
2. Run Export Script: In terminal, run:
   node scripts/export_for_github.js

This creates a folder: "export_to_github" containing the new stats.

## STEP 3: UPLOAD TO GITHUB

1. F1-Telemetry Repo: Push your edited config files.
2. f1-telemetry-api Repo: Upload files from "export_to_github" folder:
   - drivers/*.json -> GitHub drivers/
   - constructors/2026/*.json -> GitHub constructors/2026/
3. f1aapi Repo: Upload results.json (and drivers.json if needed).
4. f2api Repo: Upload results.json (and drivers.json if needed).

## STEP 4: CLEAR LIVE CACHE

Visit the live site with ?admin=true and click the "Refresh Data" button:
